==History==
2016 
*The Poison [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 29/2/2016, in the [[Version History#March 2016 Update (29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]].
*On 23/3/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (23/3/2016)|Balance Update]], increased the Poison's damage by 5%.
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], changed the description of the Poison. The description prior to this update was "''Covers the target area in a sticky toxin, damaging and slowing down troops and buildings. Remember: solvent abuse can kill!''"
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments%20Update%20(4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], allowed the [[Elixir Collector]] to be affected by the Poison's slowing.
*On 20/10/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (20/10/2016)|Balance Update]], removed the Poison's slowing capabilities. This also changed the description. It was used to say: "''Covers the target area in a sticky toxin, damaging and slowing down enemy troops and buildings. Yet somehow leaves the grass green and healthy. Go figure!''"
*On 30/11/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (30/11/2016)|Balance Update]], increased the Poison's damage by 10%.
2017
*On 13/2/2017, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (13/2/2017)|Balance Update]], decreased the Poison's duration to 8 seconds (from 10 seconds), but increased its damage by 24%.
*On 12/6/2017, the [[Version History#June 2017 Update (12/6/2017)|June 2017 Update]] allowed multiple Poison [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] to stack.
*On 12/12/2017, the [[Version History#Electrifying Update (12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]], decreased the Poison’s [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]] damage to 35% of the full damage (from 40%).
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], allowed the Poison to be placed on the river.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 1/10/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|Balance Update]], fixed a bug where [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that were spawned after their parent troops died would be immune to spell damage.
2020
*On 4/8/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/8/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Poison’s Crown Tower damage to 30% of the full damage (from 35%).
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Poison from Spell Valley to Jungle Arena. It also slightly changed the Poison's description, adding the phrase "''Reduced damage to Crown Towers.''" to it.
*On 6/9/2021, the [[Version History#2021%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(6/9/2021)|2021 Quarter 3 Update]], allowed the Poison to slow enemies' speed by 15%.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 14/5/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (14/5/2024)|Balance Update]], decreased the Poison’s Crown Tower damage to 25% of the full damage (from 30%).
2025
*On 4/2/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/2/2025)|Balance Update]], made it so that [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack Ghost]] is immune to Poison.
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Poison's damage by 1.09%.
2026

* On 1/6/2026, a Balance Update, decreased the Poison’s Crown Tower damage to 23% of the full damage (from 25%)

