== Trivia== 
*The Poison resembles the real life chemical [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bromine Bromine (Br)], a halogen that, at room temperature, is a rapidly evaporating red-orange liquid just like the Poison.
*The Poison is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Heal]], [[Lightning]], [[Freeze]], [[Rage]], and [[Clone]].
**In Clash of Clans, the container for Poison resemble spells that take up 1 housing space, which is similar to its Clash Royale counterpart.
**Unlike its [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Spell Clash of Clans counterpart], Poison in Clash Royale does affect [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], has no damage-scaling effects and does not affect the opposing [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]]' attack speed.
**In Clash Royale, the liquid of Poison is colored red whereas in Clash of Clans, the liquid is colored orange.
*The Poison is the first spell to be added to the game after Clash Royale's release.
*In the Korean, Chinese, and Thai language settings of the game, the Poison's name translates to "Poison Magic", "Damage Potion Spell", and "Venom" respectively.
*The Poison is 1 of 7 spells which have team-colored rings on their radius, the others are Earthquake, Freeze, Rage, Clone, [[Tornado]], and [[Graveyard]].
*It is 1 of 12 cards that is unavailable in [[Chess Royale]], the others being [[Royal Recruits]], [[Rocket]], Earthquake, Lightning, [[Goblin Drill]], [[Miner]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], and the [[Monk]].
*While not available as a spell, the Poison's sounds are featured in the [https://beatstar.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Theme Clash of Clans Theme] [https://beatstar.fandom.com/wiki/Songs song] in Beatstar.
*Due to censorship laws, in the Chinese version of the game, the Poison is recolored green, though the background remains unchanged.
*The Poison was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Poison was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/DVY2TndGf4U?si=ptuVz0tHkkkDIvEl Crown Championship Global Series Tournament], by a player called Sergioramos:).
**The Poison was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/cmBlEI-aDoo?si=UoD1Sit2YvQR19xs Clash Royale League 2019 Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Poison was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/nMANpDweTA4?si=nsUAou7ny3WAA2ve Clash Royale League 2022 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
**The Poison was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/vRrgTfqRdpw?si=YDASUydL7qNm9QZz Clash Royale League 2023 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*On 6/6/2023, the Poison was supposed to receive a Crown Tower Damage decrease to 25% (from 30%), but this change [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-48-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].
*Before the Poison's card release, the Poison's damage was decreased by 11%.

